## Files

New (only new files, plus the plan's two declared additive build exceptions):

- `src/cljc/yin/repl/core.cljc` — the local shell as one explicit immutable value: VM, lang, value history, v2 output medium + minted cursor, and a per-medium **last-outcome ledger** with `:untried` (so `repl-state` never asks a handle whether it is closed — v2 has no `closed?`). `drain-output` is total over `ok/blocked/gap/end/cursor-mismatch/invalid-cursor/transport-error`, advances only to the exact successor a handle returns, and is bounded by a read budget. `(vm :type)` accepts `:ast-walker` only; `(telemetry)` is answered with a rejection naming `yin.repl`; datom-literal input is answered with its unmet prerequisite instead of being wired to a v1 stream.
- `src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc` — `repl-step [state now]`, the sole owner of REPL and RPC state. Drains the composition-owned input ring buffer (capacity 1024, cursor held only here), evaluates local input, forwards ordinary source through `yin.repl-adapter`/`dao.stream.rpc`, publishes completions **exactly once** into an outbox, and returns the next state. Never loops on `blocked`; no promise, future, callback, atom, global, or clock. One outstanding remote request at a time — later lines queue instead of clobbering (v1's race at `repl.cljc:1044`), while `help`, `repl-state`, `quit`, `disconnect`, `connect` bypass the queue. A `full` writer retries the *same* already-allocated envelope. Input `gap` publishes a loss notice, resumes at the recovery cursor, and evaluates none of the evicted lines.
- `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc` — host entry points. clj: reader thread parks in `read-line` and only appends; one owned poller thread carries the state value through serial `repl-step` calls. cljs (Node): readline handler only appends; one `setInterval` owner. cljd: stdin listener only appends; one `Timer.periodic` owner. `--port`/`--host`/`--headless` parse as in v1; `--telemetry`/`--telemetry-stream` are rejected by name.
- `src/clj/yin/repl/runner.clj`, `bin/yin_repl_main.dart` — the cljd entry point.
- Tests: `test/yin/repl_core_test.cljc`, `v2_driver_test.cljc`, `v2_test.cljc`, `v2_build_test.clj`.
- `deps.edn` (+4 aliases: `:clj-yin-repl`, `:cljs-yin-repl`, `:cljd-yin-repl`, `:cljd-yin-repl-build`) and `shadow-cljs.edn` (+`:yin-repl` `:node-script`) — purely additive; `v2_build_test.clj` asserts every v1 alias/build is unchanged.

Not touched: `yin/repl.cljc`, `src/clj/yin/repl/runner.clj`, `dao.stream` v1, docs, collab. Nothing staged or committed. (`src/cljc/dao/stream/rpc/ws.cljc` and `test/dao/stream/rpc_ws_test.cljc` appeared untracked during this session — another lane's work, untouched by me.)

